        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under dry argon using Schlenk techniques, a toluene (20.0 mL) solution of [(Me3Si)2N]3YIII(μ-Cl)Li(THF)3 (0.829 g, 1.00 mmol) was added at room temperature to a toluene (10.0 mL) solution of ligand 1, 3-(2-C4H3NHCH=NCH2CH2)C8H5NH (0.237 g, 1.00 mmol). The mixture was heated at 75–85 °C for 72 h (color change from light brown to brown). The solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure, the residue extracted with n-hexane (2 × 10 mL), and the combined extracts concentrated to about 10.0 mL. Light brown crystals of 3a formed at 0 °C after several days.",
        "reagents": [
